casebook b-46cfr-58_25-25-steering-alarms-draft v1
source "B-46cfr-58.25-25-steering-alarms.txt" dated 2026-10-14 by "drafted by anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5 from the manual; not yet approved"
note "UNAPPROVED DRAFT: written by a language model from B-46cfr-58.25-25-steering-alarms.txt. Every declaration below cites the sentence"
note "it came from. Check each against the manual, add what the manual does not say, then delete"
note "this note to approve. quorum studio will not build a chip image while it is here."

# manual: "Failure of the electric power to the control system of any steering gear"
observe control_power_failed "electric power to the control system of a steering gear has failed"

# manual: "Failure of that power to the power unit of any steering gear"
observe power_unit_power_failed "electric power to the power unit of a steering gear has failed"

# manual: "Occurrence of a low oil level in any oil reservoir of a hydraulic, power-operated steering-gear system"
observe low_oil_reported "low oil level in a reservoir of a hydraulic, power-operated steering-gear system"

# manual: "Failure of any phase of a three-phase power supply"
observe phase_failed "a phase of a three-phase power supply has failed"

# manual: "Overload of any motor described by § 58.25-55(c)"
observe motor_overloaded "overload of a steering-gear motor"

# manual: "On each vessel of 1,600 gross tons or over, a steering-failure alarm must be provided in the pilothouse"
observe steering_failed "steering failure has occurred"

# manual: "that activates when the motor is energized"
observe motor_energized "a steering-gear power motor is energized"

# manual: "Occurrence of a low oil level in any oil reservoir of a hydraulic, power-operated steering-gear system"
claim low_oil_level "low oil level in a hydraulic steering-gear reservoir" severity 5 needs low_oil_reported

# manual: "Overload of any motor described by § 58.25-55(c)"
claim motor_overload_fault "steering-gear motor overload" severity 5 needs motor_overloaded

# manual: "On each vessel of 1,600 gross tons or over, a steering-failure alarm must be provided in the pilothouse"
claim steering_failure "steering failure on a vessel of 1,600 gross tons or over" severity 7 needs steering_failed

# manual: "that activates when the motor is energized"
claim motor_running "a steering-gear power motor is running" severity 1 needs motor_energized

# manual: "the electric power to the control system of any steering gear"
claim control_power_loss "loss of electric power to the steering gear control system" severity 6 needs control_power_failed

# manual: "that power to the power unit of any steering gear"
claim power_unit_power_loss "loss of electric power to the steering gear power unit" severity 6 needs power_unit_power_failed

# manual: "any phase of a three-phase power supply"
claim phase_loss "failure of a phase of the three-phase supply" severity 5 needs phase_failed

# manual: "An audible and a visible alarm must activate in the machinery space upon"
action alarm_machinery_space when any phase_loss motor_overload_fault low_oil_level phase_failed_blind motor_overloaded_blind

# manual: "Each power motor for the main and auxiliary steering gear must have a “motor running” indicator light in the pilothouse, and in the machinery space, that activates when the motor is energized."
action keep_running idle

# manual: "On each vessel of 1,600 gross tons or over, a steering-failure alarm must be provided in the pilothouse"
action secure_steering safe when any steering_failure steering_failed_blind

# manual: "An audible and a visible alarm must activate in the pilothouse upon"
action alarm_pilothouse when any control_power_loss power_unit_power_loss low_oil_level steering_failure control_power_failed_blind power_unit_power_failed_blind low_oil_reported_blind

# manual: "must have a “motor running” indicator light in the pilothouse, and in the machinery space"
action show_motor_running when any motor_running motor_energized_blind

# manual: "must have a “motor running” indicator light in the pilothouse, and in the machinery space"
prefer secure_steering over alarm_pilothouse over alarm_machinery_space over show_motor_running over keep_running

# ── Failed-sensor checks, added by quorum studio ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# cbc refused this rulebook because nothing could argue with any claim, so it could not tell a dead sensor
# from a quiet machine. Each block below stops claims being drawn from one reading while its instrument has
# failed, and takes the response that reading would have led to instead. Each is a suggestion: confirm or
# delete it.

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the control_power_failed instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that alarm_pilothouse is the right response then. If control_power_failed is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe control_power_failed_failed "the instrument behind control_power_failed has failed or is disconnected"
doubt control_power_failed_untrusted "control_power_failed is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs control_power_failed_failed
control_power_failed_untrusted undercuts control_power_loss
claim control_power_failed_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of control_power_failed" needs control_power_failed_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the power_unit_power_failed instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that alarm_pilothouse is the right response then. If power_unit_power_failed is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe power_unit_power_failed_failed "the instrument behind power_unit_power_failed has failed or is disconnected"
doubt power_unit_power_failed_untrusted "power_unit_power_failed is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs power_unit_power_failed_failed
power_unit_power_failed_untrusted undercuts power_unit_power_loss
claim power_unit_power_failed_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of power_unit_power_failed" needs power_unit_power_failed_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the low_oil_reported instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that alarm_pilothouse is the right response then. If low_oil_reported is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe low_oil_reported_failed "the instrument behind low_oil_reported has failed or is disconnected"
doubt low_oil_reported_untrusted "low_oil_reported is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs low_oil_reported_failed
low_oil_reported_untrusted undercuts low_oil_level
claim low_oil_reported_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of low_oil_reported" needs low_oil_reported_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the phase_failed instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that alarm_machinery_space is the right response then. If phase_failed is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe phase_failed_failed "the instrument behind phase_failed has failed or is disconnected"
doubt phase_failed_untrusted "phase_failed is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs phase_failed_failed
phase_failed_untrusted undercuts phase_loss
claim phase_failed_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of phase_failed" needs phase_failed_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the motor_overloaded instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that alarm_machinery_space is the right response then. If motor_overloaded is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe motor_overloaded_failed "the instrument behind motor_overloaded has failed or is disconnected"
doubt motor_overloaded_untrusted "motor_overloaded is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs motor_overloaded_failed
motor_overloaded_untrusted undercuts motor_overload_fault
claim motor_overloaded_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of motor_overloaded" needs motor_overloaded_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the steering_failed instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that secure_steering is the right response then. If steering_failed is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe steering_failed_failed "the instrument behind steering_failed has failed or is disconnected"
doubt steering_failed_untrusted "steering_failed is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs steering_failed_failed
steering_failed_untrusted undercuts steering_failure
claim steering_failed_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of steering_failed" needs steering_failed_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the motor_energized instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that show_motor_running is the right response then. If motor_energized is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe motor_energized_failed "the instrument behind motor_energized has failed or is disconnected"
doubt motor_energized_untrusted "motor_energized is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs motor_energized_failed
motor_energized_untrusted undercuts motor_running
claim motor_energized_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of motor_energized" needs motor_energized_failed
